WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back. We're here
with Senator Bernie Sanders.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.071
You were with President Biden
at his inauguration,

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:06.406
and you became a meme.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.207
We've talked about you
and your mittens.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.142
-Yeah.
-I'd heard you lost the mittens,

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.912
but then I realized -- not true.
-Not true. Fake news.

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:15.548
-Fake news. But there's a reason
we don't see the mittens.

00:00:15.614 --> 00:00:17.417
-My wife is
hiding them away someplace.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.118
-Yeah.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.221 align:end size:97% position:97%
She worried you're getting
too involved in social media,

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.056
becoming a meme?
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.424
-So she's hid the mittens,
and that's why we don't see

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.925
the mittens.
-It's gonna be a legacy

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:27.226
for the grandchildren.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.661
-Right. Those mittens
are going to be worth

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.064
a lot of scratch
when the time comes.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.798
I know you have a lot

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:35.802
of immense personal respect
for President Biden.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.737
Obviously, we have
an election coming up.

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.406
The Democratic voting coalition
is very diverse.

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:42.341
A lot of different kinds
of people.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.942
Make a case for why

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:48.347
you think people should turn out
for President Biden in November.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:51.184
-Well, for a first step,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.520
it's absolutely imperative
that Donald Trump be defeated.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.088
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.155 --> 00:01:00.226
And it's -- let me, you know --
and what this election is about,

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.627
it is not just policy.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:05.164
It's not just differences
of views on health care,

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.434
education, or tax policy.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.837
You have a president,
former president,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.406
who really does not believe
in democracy.

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.941
He's trying to
undermine democracy.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:19.245
He is a pathological liar.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:23.449
And he is,
in very intense ways,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.418
trying to divide our people up.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:29.054
Look, this country faces
enormous problems today,

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.523
and we all know what they are.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.525
We're talking about income
and wealth inequality.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.694
We're talking about
60% of workers

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.963
living paycheck to paycheck.
We're talking about

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.632
the existential
threat of climate change.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.967
Enormous problems
facing this country.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.869
But instead of focusing

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.372
and providing solutions
to those problems,

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.876
what Trump is trying to do
is get us to hate each other

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.444
based on where we were born,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.115
or the color of our skin
or our sexual orientation,

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:58.484
and we just cannot
allow that to happen.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:02.054
And then on top of all that,
you got a guy in Trump

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.322
who, during his presidency,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.158
gave massive tax breaks
to the rich at a time

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.627
when we have unprecedented
income and wealth inequality.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:09.963
It's the last thing they need.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.332
This guy wants to throw
tens of millions of people

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.701
off of the health insurance
that they have.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:19.572
He appointed anti-union
members of his administration

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:21.807
to make it harder
for workers to form unions.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.709
And I'll tell you,
all over this country,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.079
women are fighting for the right
to control their own bodies.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.349
He wants to take that away.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.785
So that's Trump.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.786
And on the other hand,
in Biden --

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.421
I'm not going to sit here.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.089
You know, I ran against Biden,
so I'm not going to sit here

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.258
and tell you that I agree with
everything Joe Biden is doing.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.928
I don't, big time.
But on the other hand,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.997
this is the first president in
the history of the United States

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:48.901
to walk on a picket line
with workers.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.003
And that's a pretty
impressive thing.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.972
We've made some progress

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.641
in lowering the cost
of prescription drugs

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.676
and taking on
the pharmaceutical industry.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:59.445
The economy,
as you've indicated,

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.115
is really doing well.
Unemployment extremely low.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.516
We're creating
a whole lot of jobs,

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.285
rebuilding manufacturing
in America.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.654
So we're beginning to move
forward in the right direction.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.290
In my view, we have a lot,
lot more to do.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.861
But the choice in this election
is very clear.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.329
If you do not believe
in democracy,

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:20.032
if you really want to turn
your back on the millions of men

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.935
and women
who fought to defend democracy,

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:27.207
I guess Trump is your candidate.
But if you believe in

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.208
what this country
is supposed to value,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.910
is that we all come together
as one people,

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:35.781
we believe in the rule of law,
Biden is your candidate.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.217
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.685
-I want to ask,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.989
because I know you've been
a voice in the Senate

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.890
over the current situation
in the Middle East.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:48.361
We are almost four months
after the horrifically

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.530
unforgivable acts
of October 7th.

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:54.133
You've called Hamas a disgusting
terrorist organization.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.768
Many hostages are not back.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.637
And yet we also see
an unspeakable loss

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:01.273
of civilian lives in Gaza.
Is there --

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.577
Do you have any optimism for
a peaceful future for Israelis?

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.279
-I hope to God it takes place.

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:09.148
And as you've just indicated,

00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:12.785
Hamas began this war
with their horrific,

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:15.554
brutal terrorist attack
against --

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:18.424
killing 1,200 innocent Israelis,

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.494
wounding more, taking over
200 people hostage.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.862
But I have to tell you
that what Netanyahu

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.733
and his right wing government
are doing right now

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:31.637
to the people of Palestine
is -- of Gaza

00:04:31.703 --> 00:04:35.307
is indescribable
and unspeakable.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:36.876
I mean, we're looking at 25--

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:40.279
26,000 people who have been
killed already,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.448
two-thirds of whom
are women and children,

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:45.651
65,000 people
who have been wounded.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:50.389
We're looking at 70%
of the housing units in Gaza

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.492
have been damaged or destroyed.
Can you believe that?

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.161
70%? You're looking
at 1.8 million people

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:58.097
pushed out of their homes.
God knows where they're going.

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:01.601
And right now, and this is --
I hope everybody hears this.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.702
You're looking
at the possibility

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:08.274
of hundreds of thousands
of children starving to death.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.743
And we in the United States,

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:13.612
through our financial
support of Israel,

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:15.814
are complicit
in what's happening.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:19.185
And I will be damned if I'm
going to give another nickel

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:22.221
to the Netanyahu government
in order to continue this war

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.891
against the Palestinian people.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:30.863
-Do you see --
I mean, it all seems so, uh --

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.632
impossible --
I mean, I certainly don't know

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.602
the solution
I wouldn't ever claim to,

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.171
but do you see any hope
for optimism

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.508
that there's a future for the
Palestinians and the Israelis?

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.677
-The history
of the region is terrible.

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.378
You know, we don't have the time
to go into it.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.148
Deals with the Holocaust,
6 million Jews.

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.950
It deals with the displacement

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:54.519
of hundreds of thousands
of Palestinians from their home.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:59.225
But at the end of the day,
the people, Palestinian people

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:02.328
are entitled
to a homeland of their own.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.496
So we're talking about
a two-state solution.

00:06:04.563 --> 00:06:07.666
Hamas cannot be, in my view,
part of that equation.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.102
They are a terrorist
jihadist group.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:14.273
There are people, Palestinians,
who believe in democracy,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.074
Palestinians who do believe

00:06:16.141 --> 00:06:18.478
in improving the lives
of people there.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:19.979
We've got to work
with those people

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:22.014
and create
a long term solution

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.384
where Israel has the security
that it is entitled to

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.886
and the Palestinians
have a state of their own

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:30.055
and the freedom
that they are entitled to.

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:32.791
-Well, we really appreciate
any time

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.994
you make time for us.
It is such a pleasure.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.262
Thank you so much,
Senator Sanders.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:37.363
-Thank you.
-Senator Bernie Sanders,

00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:38.964
everybody.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.666
"It's OK to be Angry
About Capitalism"

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.034
is in paperback
February 20th.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.202
-We'll be right back
with Zosia Mamet.

